=== Regex ===
+ Regular Expressions are custom patterns to be found within a text (PatternMatcherTest01.java is showing how to use)
+ Use RegExr
+ Caution with case sensitive (a/A, b/B)

== Metacharacters ==
+ Useful to find determined characters (use \\ to scape)

\d -> Digit
\D -> Isn't digit
\s -> Space
\S -> Isn't space
\w -> a-zA-Z, digit and  _ (special characters)
\W -> Isn't a-zA-Z, digit and  _

[] -> Range (in range of... like: "[a-zA-Z] or [0-9]")

$ -> End of the line
. -> Joker (1.3 = 123, 1@3, 1L3)

^ -> Matches from the begging of the string, while finding the parameters
[^] -> Denial if is into a range, like: "[^a-z]+" = everything isn't a-z

() -> Grouping expressions to use modifiers
| -> Or, like this: "o(v|c)o" ovo | oco

= Quantifiers =
Expression quantifier

? -> 0 or 1 occurrence
* -> 0 or more occurrences
+ -> 1 or more occurrences
{n, m} -> from n to m occurrences
